-Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub. The host is moving to
+A 19-language override layer for DSH i18n (ja/ko/fr/...), shipped as a
+client-only plugin: the browser half intercepts the locale runtime's lookup
+chain so a selected third language wins over DSH's native zh/en while DSH's
+active locale stays on `en`, ships a custom switcher row into the settings
+General section, and persists the selection in localStorage
+(`dsh-plugin-better-locale:active`). It also publishes `ctx.betterLocale` so
+other plugins can register their own dictionaries for the new languages.
+Client-only plugin — the host half is a no-op stub. The host target is
 dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2.
 
+Migration note (0.1.1-era style → dsh 0.1.2-alpha.2): the cohort changed the
+intercepted method's signature, and it also grew an official language-pack API.
+The two facts pull in opposite directions, so this migration separates them:
+
+- **The interception is rebased, not retired.** `LocaleRuntime.lookup` now
+  takes `(ns, key, chain)`; the old two-argument wrapper makes the original
+  method iterate `undefined` and throws `TypeError: chain is not iterable` on
+  every key the override store misses. The wrapper now forwards `chain`, so it
+  works on the alpha.2 cohort and still tolerates a two-argument host.
+- **The official catalog API is not this plugin's entry point.** On
+  alpha.2, `ctx.locale.addLanguage({ id, label, fallback })` plus the
+  single-locale `ctx.locale.register(ns, locale, dict)` register languages and
+  dictionaries in the harness's own Language row (the same
+  `settings.general.item` slot) and persist the choice as `locale.preference`
+  in `$DSH_HOME/settings.yaml`. Selecting one of those languages there makes it
+  DSH's **active** locale: DSH's own copy then resolves through that language's
+  fallback chain and `<html lang>` follows it. This plugin's documented
+  behavior is the opposite — a third language overlays the UI while the active
+  locale stays `en` and the native zh/en behavior is never taken over — so the
+  harness does not cover this entry point. Adding the pack languages to the
+  official row as well would put the same language in two selectors with two
+  different meanings (and silently disable the overlay whenever the official
+  row won), which is why the "keep the patch AND also call addLanguage" memo
+  from the 0.1.x era is deliberately not followed.
+- **Official extension points that are the same entry point are used.** Every
+  registration is an owned `ctx.effect` (HMR/disposal removes exactly what was
+  added); the switcher row's own copy namespace goes through the harness
+  dictionary registry (`ctx.locale.register(NS, { zh, en })`) and the row
+  registers into the additive `settings.general.item` list slot with a fresh id
+  and the `locale:` seat; the bundle stays a self-contained `dsh.bundle.patch`
+  row with a `dsh.client` manifest and a complete `exports` map.
+- **The remaining gap is upstream.** There is no official extension point for a
+  non-mutating overlay (an added language whose dictionaries are consulted
+  before the active locale's chain) and no public way to republish the locale
+  revision after such a selection, so the plugin still intercepts the private
+  `lookup` and calls the private `publish(active, true)`. Those two private
+  touches are the migration's residual harness dependency.
+
 Release procedure (internal):
 
 1. Apply the migration changes.
